A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when evidence supports the **same failing path**
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause)). This replaces the subject-only
rule in the preserved historical [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).

1. Read the body and look up the tenant's locale, form version and channel.
2. Compare the failing path with an open ticket, checking contradictory symptoms.
3. Merge only a supported match. Otherwise keep a separate ticket or investigate missing context.
4. Count unique report IDs; preserve received and merged timestamps separately.

<Callout>
Same subjects can hide different failures; different subjects can describe the same one.
The #4471 review shows how subject-only merging hid the booking-form hint problem.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Investigate. Unknown tenants and contradictory bodies are not established duplicates.
See the [#4471 review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) for evidence and the two ticket paths.
